      "designator": "CS23-0",
      "grouping_at_time": "Subpart D \u2014 Design And Construction",
      "title_at_revision": "Nose/tail-wheel steering",
      "text": "(a) If nose/tail-wheel steering is installed, it must be demonstrated that its use does not require exceptional pilot skill during take-off and landing, in cross-winds and in the event of an engine failure or its use must be limited to low speed manoeuvring. (b) Movement of the pilots steering control must not interfere with correct retraction or extension of the landing gear.",
